  "epc_number": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed rear dormer infill extension by virtue of its design, scale, siting, dimensions and awkward relationship with the existing two storey rear roof projections would give rise to a contrived and bulky form of development that would be detrimental to the visual amenities of Montagu Road. Additionally, the dormer infill extension would create additional bulk to the roofscape to represent a dominant and incongruous addition and awkward relationship with the parent roof slope, thereby both unbalancing and detracting from the character and symmetry of the prevailing build form within the street scene and the terrace of which the site forms a part. The proposal would therefore fail to preserve the character and appearance of the application dwelling and the wider setting, contrary to Policy D3 of the London Plan (2021), CP30 of the Core Strategy, DMD8, DMD13 and DMD37 of the Development Management Document as well as the aims and intentions outlined within the NPPF (2024).",
    "The proposed development, by virtue of the insufficient  head height for Flat 3 at loft level, would result in a sub-standard form of accommodation that would not be able to cater for the reasonable needs of future occupiers, contrary to Policy D6 of the London Plan 2021, Policies CP4 and CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy 2010, Policy DMD8 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), the Nationally Described Space Standard (2015) as well as the NPPF (2024)."
  ],
